Healers can become Expert in the healing spell school,
costing 3 slots.  Well worth doing as offered.  Healing,
cure blindness, cure sickness, extra healing, stone to
flesh, restore ability.  Some wonderfull, some not,
some available through a unihorn.  It's very nice to
not have to rely on a unihorn that could end up cursed.
Even better, when spellbooks are generated as prayer
gifts the game searches for ones in your schools so
there is a very high chance that a healer will end up
knowing all of those.

Healers can become Skilled at Dagger, Expert at knife.
Very tempting to take up throwing several knives in
the same turn.  Knives suck as weapons so enchanting a
large stack matters very much.  But this does mean
you'll never be able to throw several daggers per
turn so knives are your missiles not daggers.

Healers can get to Expert at quarterstaff, just right
for their Quest artifact.  Worth using a mundane
quarterstaff as a melee weapon at least sometimes
before then.  Unihorn similar comments.

If I read the table correctly healers are always
neutral.  Being neutral, healers can get Magicbane,
Mojo and/or Vorpy.

Stepping back and looking through this, I worry about
the late game problems of twohanded weapons and look to
Magicbane.  I'd be inclined to hoard all knife class
weapons for throwing, advance knife class to Expert,
enchant a big stack of knives.  Since Magicbane could
appear later I'd get Sting from the first non-cursed
elven dagger and use it enough to move towards Skilled.
Also use my starting spells regularly to advance to
Expert in healing (making the mines easier to survive).

For melee weapons it would be a trade-off: Depend on
what artifacts arrive from altar camping or go mostly
non-artifact focusing on getting fixed crysknife.
Explore wielding Sting early and Magicbane mid/late
game.  Fight using either a fixed crysknife or whatever
other good artifact is given.  Use "x" to swap from
exploration to combat.  Because of the guaranteed
altar in the mines and how deep worms appear, a game
with a coaligned mine town altar would be an artifact
game for me.

Throw knives, cast unskilled attack spells at monsters,
cast expert healing spells at self and pets.


